		{
			dependencies: ["63465F6B67C8633A"]
			description: [
				"# Molecular Sequence Rewrite Array"
				""
				"The &3&lMolecular Sequence Rewrite Array&r is a high-throughput &b&lautocrafting&r machine."
				"It stores encoded patterns like a &b&lPattern Provider&r, but performs every molecular-assembler-compatible recipe inside the block instead of sending ingredients to adjacent machines."
				""
				"## Setup"
				""
				"Complete &2&lStage II: Sequence Array&r once in the &2&lMatter Fabrication Well&r, then produce this machine there."
				"Deep research improves its well manufacturing recipe, not the performance of the placed array."
				""
				"1. Connect the array to a powered &b&lME Network&r with an available channel."
				"2. Right-click it and insert encoded &b&lcrafting&r, &b&lsmithing&r, or &b&lstonecutting&r patterns."
				"3. Use the page buttons to move through the fixed pattern inventory: &e&l10 pages&r with &e&l36 slots&r each, for a total of &e&l360 pattern slots&r."
				"4. Request one of the encoded results from an &b&lME terminal&r as usual."
				""
				"Processing patterns are not executed internally."
				"Use a normal &b&lPattern Provider&r and an external machine for those."
				""
				"## Processing and outputs"
				""
				"The array uses virtual parallel processing and can finish supported recipes in as little as &e&l1 tick&r."
				"Actual throughput still depends on available ingredients, &b&lME power&r, and whether the network can accept the results."
				""
				"Recipe results, intermediate products, and container remainders are aggregated by AE key and returned to the &b&lME Network&r."
				"If the network cannot accept them immediately, the array keeps them in a persistent output buffer and retries later, including after a world reload."
				""
				"Normal block drops retain patterns, inventory, and pending returns."
				"Replace the array and restore its &b&lME connection&r to continue."
			]
			id: "39466F9FC8385BA2"
			min_width: 450
